  "body": "MAINLINE-017b filed. From today's values (handbook gamma 0.20, wrinkle 0.33, stock panels, SR-200 faces on CR-III 5056 3/8-1.0, 028's joining replacing the 5% allowance, 019's reserve scaled by 027), P2 is 0.528 at R 10 m and 0.571 at R 20 m; global buckling binds. Only three properties reach SF 1 alone: a face 1.87/1.73 times lighter at beryllium's stiffness and strength; gamma x4.06/x3.41 (0.81/0.68, a 2.5/13 mm dimple by 015's map); face modulus x2.04/x1.93, only at the fragile Vc 2 step. Core stiffness, flatness, sheet size, film and seams are not alone. Cheapest: the lighter face alone; keeping Be, gamma alone; keeping Be and handbook values, a core stiffer than aluminium can be (product 13.1/9.5).\n\nP3 today (Ti sleeves, Kapton) is 0.710; the projection row (CFRP wrap, Zylon) floats at 1.441. Today's row reaches 1 alone on tube specific stiffness x1.41 (beyond SiC), lattice knockdown x1.99 or film specific strength x3.79. Every P3 route needs a qualified SiC compressive strength of 0.83-1.20 GPa; none exists.\n\nTrends: beryllium, aluminium honeycomb, SiC and the knockdown and wrinkling design values are flat for 30+ years; Be sheet shrank. Only film specific strength moves (2.2%/yr since 1975, 4.1% since 1999): Upilex-S gives x2.17 already, the rest in 14-25 years if it held (PROJECTION). Closest: P3 via film. Step changes: the lighter face, tube stiffness, a large-sphere knockdown, a stiffer core, lattice tests. 34 reproduction checks pass; 15 NFI rows; files pinned. The brief names no next job.",
